part soc_1
  tally 2
  law
  note "SOC-1 · An employee's social contributions: pension 9.50 %, disability 1.50 %, sickness 2.45 % of gross pay (.1); pension and disability only on the year's gross from one employer up to SOC-CAP, in the crossing month on the part up to it (.2); each contribution of a month rounded to the ort, half up (.3, GEN-5 .3). Parental pay and pensions bear none."

source soc_1 "Social Insurance Act, SOC-1 An employee's social contributions (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

index soc1_part = [pension, disability, sickness]

input soc1_er_pension: num question "What is the employer's own pension contribution rate (SOC-1 .4)?"

input soc1_rate[c in soc1_part]: num question "What is the employee's rate of this contribution (SOC-1 .1)?"

input soc_cap: money DUK question "What is this year's SOC-CAP (SOC-1 .2)?"

version soc1_v1
  cite soc_1
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-09-01
  note "SOC-1 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-09-01; governs pay paid from 2018-01-01."
